   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the sale of hookahs, shisha and water pipes to minors",
    "basePrintNo": "S4269",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4269-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1399-aa & 1399-cc, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4269\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn  act  to  amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the\nsale of hookahs, shisha and water pipes to minors\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis Bill would prohibit the sale  of  tobacco  products,  herbal  ciga-\nrettes,  shishas,  rolling paper or smoking paraphernalia to minors. Any\nperson operating a place of business wherein  tobacco  products,  herbal\ncigarettes  or shishas, are sold or offered for sale may only sell these\nproducts to individuals who are at least eighteen years of age and  with\nproper identification.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection  1399-cc  of the public health law, as amended by chapter 508 of\nthe laws of 200, subdivision 3 as separately amended by chapter  508  of\nthe  laws  of  200 and chapter 1G2 of the laws of 2002, subdivision 7 as\namended by chapter 13 of the laws of 2003 is amended.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nDue to the negative health effects of these products it is important  to\nemphasize  the seriousness the health risks to the public and especially\nto the youth. This bill would help to control and limit the sale of  the\nhookah  products and smoking paraphernalia to the minors that would face\nserious health risks by smoking the products listed above.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
