    "lawCode": "Amd §§1399-aa & 1399-cc, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4269A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the sale of\nhookahs, shisha and water pipes to minors\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis Bill would prohibit the sale of\ntobacco products, herbal cigarettes, shishas, rolling paper or\nsmoking paraphernalia to minors. Any person operating a place of\nbusiness wherein tobacco products, herbal cigarettes or shishas, are\nsold or offered for sale may only sell these products to individuals\nwho are at least eighteen years of age and with proper identification.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1399-cc of the public health law, as amended by chapter 508\nof the laws of 2000, subdivision 3 as separately amended by chapter 508\nof the laws of 2000 and chapter 162 of the\nlaws of 2002, subdivision 7 as amended by chapter 13\nof the laws of 2003 is amended.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nDue to the negative health effects of these products it\nis important to emphasize the seriousness the health risks to the\npublic and especially to the youth. This bill would help to control\nand limit the sale of the hookah products and smoking paraphernalia\nto the minors that would face serious health risks by smoking the\nproducts listed above.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of January next succeeding\nthe date on which it shall become law.\n\n",
