    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4269B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the sale of\nhookahs, shisha and water pipes to minors\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis Bill would prohibit the sale of tobacco products, herbal\ncigarettes, shishas, rolling paper or smoking paraphernalia to\nminors. Any person operating a place of business wherein tobacco\nproducts, herbal cigarettes or shishas, are sold or offered for sale\nmay only sell these products to individuals who are at least eighteen\nyears of age and with proper identification.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nsection 1399-cc of the public health law, as amended by chapter 508 of\nthe laws of 2000, subdivision 3 as separately amended by chapter 508\nof the laws of 2000 and chapter 162 of the laws of 2002, subdivision\n7 as amended by chapter 13 of the laws of 2003 is amended.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nDue to the negative health effects of these products it is important\nto emphasize the seriousness the health risks to the public and\nespecially to the youth. This bill would help to control and limit\nthe sale of the hookah products and smoking paraphernalia to the\nminors that would face serious health risks by smoking the products\nlisted above.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of January next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall become law.\n\n",
